---
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro'
import site from '../data/site.json'
const E = site.email
---
<Legal title="Accessibility statement" description="Redbarn Ventures' commitment to an accessible website for everyone, the standards we follow and how to report a problem." lead="Last updated 20 November 2026. We want everyone to be able to use this website, whatever their device, ability or circumstances.">
  <section><h2>Our commitment</h2><p>Redbarn Ventures is committed to making redbarn.ventures accessible and usable for as many people as possible. We design and build with accessibility in mind from the start, and we apply the same standards to the websites we build for clients.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Standards we follow</h2><p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. These internationally recognised guidelines explain how to make web content more accessible to people with a wide range of disabilities.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What we have done</h2><ul><li>Clear page structure with meaningful headings, landmarks and a skip-to-content link.</li><li>Full keyboard navigation, including menus, forms and pop-ups, with visible focus states.</li><li>Text and interface colours chosen for strong contrast.</li><li>Descriptive labels for form fields and clear error messages.</li><li>Text alternatives for meaningful graphics and diagrams; decorative graphics are hidden from screen readers.</li><li>Respect for the "reduce motion" setting: animations, the loading screen and scrolling effects are switched off for visitors who ask for less motion.</li><li>Layouts that adapt to small screens and to browser zoom up to 200 percent.</li></ul></section>
  <section><h2>Known limitations</h2><p>Some decorative illustrations and animated diagrams convey mood rather than information; where they contain information, we provide a text description. Links to third-party services, such as LinkedIn, are outside our control and may not meet the same standards.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Feedback</h2><p>If you have difficulty using any part of this website, or have suggestions for improvement, please email <a href={`mailto:${E}`}>{E}</a>. Tell us the page, the problem and the technology you were using, and we will do our best to respond quickly and provide the information in another format if needed.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Ongoing improvement</h2><p>We review accessibility whenever we add new pages or features, and we test with keyboard navigation, screen readers and automated tools as part of our regular quality checks.</p></section>
</Legal>
